<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile receives five bidders for spot tin.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile receives five bidders for spot tin.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Defense National Stockpile Center said it received bids from five companies for spot tin on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cambridge Street Metal bid for 10 tonnes at $2.50 a lb.</p>
<p>RMT Metals bid for 200 tonnes at $2.51.</p>
<p>Baron Metals &amp; Alloys bid for 40 tonnes at $2.4929.</p>
<p>American Iron &amp; Metal bid for 180 tonnes at $2.4857 to $2.4925.</p>
<p>Ney Smelting bid for 20 tonnes at $2.448.</p>
<p>The award was due soon.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
